      "text": "Buenos Aires to Mendoza"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e3ac0e52cf07f4f5a529d8da63105fd930c9be1de13ef2924eb782c1773f7974",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw8vu04w",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Mendoza. On arrival, you’ll be met and taken to your hotel.\n\nThen head out on a city tour. Founded in the 16th century, Mendoza was originally part of Chile. A major earthquake in the 19th century destroyed almost all of the old city. The ruins of the Church of San Francisco are among the few surviving traces of the original settlement.\n\nDespite its dry climate, Mendoza is a very green city. Around 80,000 trees have been planted here, and an extensive network of canals runs through the city.\n\nYou’ll walk through Plaza España and Plaza Independencia, visit General San Martín Park and see Cerro de la Gloria, where a monument honours José de San Martín. The hill offers panoramic views over the city.\n\nThe tour lasts about 3 hours."
    },
